title: '''contains'' = ''presents'' = ''shows'''
pid: 5135c7c8-0ec9-4c65-b5f0-c63a722664da
body: |2-
  The code only uses 'contains',
  but the user should think 'presents', 'shows'.
  Each container presents its contents.
  It wants the user to see them.

  This contrasts with links,
  which it only offers to the user.
  The user must choose to consciously follow a link;
  the presented contents, by contrast,
  begin in the buffer (unless their presenting viewnode
  is a readonly stub).
